      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-269753",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the functions $y: R^{3} \u2192 R \\cdot [- 1, 1]$ and $f: R^{2} \u2192 R^{2}$, defined by\n$y(x) = \\begin{bmatrix}x_{1} + x_{2}x_{3} \\\\ \\cos (x_{1} + x_{2} + x_{3})\\end{bmatrix}.f(y) = \\begin{bmatrix}2y_{1} + 5y_{2} \\\\ y_{1}y_{2}^{3}\\end{bmatrix}$\nAccording to the chain rule, the derivative\n$\\frac{d}{dx}f(y(x))$\nis the product of a {{field-1}} $\\cdot$ {{field-2}}\nmatrix with a\n{{field-3}} $\\cdot$ {{field-4}}\nmatrix, which results in a\n{{field-5}} $\\cdot$ {{field-6}}\nmatrix."
