      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-269768",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the functions $y: R^{2} \u2192 R^{2}$ and $f: R^{2} \u2192 R^{3}$, defined by\n$y(x) = \\begin{bmatrix}x_{2} \\\\ -x_{1}\\end{bmatrix}, f(y) = \\begin{bmatrix}y_{1} \\\\ y_{2} \\\\ y_{1}y_{2}\\end{bmatrix}$.\nAccording to the chain rule, the derivative\n$\\frac{d}{dx}f(y(x))$\nis the product of a {{field-1}} $\\cdot$ {{field-2}}\nmatrix with a\n{{field-3}} $\\cdot$ {{field-4}}\nmatrix, which results in a\n{{field-5}} $\\cdot$ {{field-6}}\nmatrix."
